    <!-- Real Estate Coach Callout -->
    <div class="coach-callout">
      <h3>💡 Real Estate Coach's Take</h3>
      <p>
        Keep soil plumes in practical perspective. Historical copper smelters in Ruston (Tacoma) and Northeast Everett operated for decades during the 20th century, carrying microscopic trace particles of arsenic and lead downwind into topsoil across parts of King and Snohomish counties. However, for 95% of homeowners, this is completely manageable in daily life. Any remaining contamination is strictly confined to the top 0 to 6 inches of unpaved, bare dirt. Maintaining healthy lawn grass, using raised beds with fresh soil for vegetable gardens, wiping muddy pet paws, and taking off shoes at the door completely eliminate risk. In addition, Washington State offers <strong>free soil sampling and free soil replacement</strong> for eligible residential yards in high-priority zones.
      </p>
    </div>

